  "designNotes": "Revision 2 for 25-45 s only, rebuilt from the combined evidence c84a84257355a2ae2f83, not from the rejected 69-single skeleton. Two coordinated hand roles: a support hand on offbeat co-attacks of independently accepted upper/drum/bass events plus explicitly labelled drum/bass-role taps, and an upper hand on upper attacks. Chords mark measured co-attacks with strong upper change (CE0079/CE0129 are upper-only phrase-start accents; CE0154 is a drum/bass landing). Recurring rising-bin families reuse shapes where hand flow allows: 79-82 high stab [1,3], 72 stab [0,2], 69/70 resolution [1,2], 75-band block [0,3] with lane 3 held. Six holds follow upper-source bands that persist in before/after bins: 67 band in bar 28, 68 band in bars 29-30, two one-beat 75 blocks in bar 32, and the low 56 band in bars 33-34 split at its measured re-rise. The climax has no hold because no band there persists beyond about 3 ticks. Arc: offbeat groove -> drum fill and held texture with backbeat -> accent bars -> held low band under upper texture -> syncopated upper and two rising-sweep stairs -> offbeat stab-chain climax. Lane directions are hand-flow choices or contour hypotheses from rising bins and visible sweeps, never certified pitch. No audio listening was performed.",
